// The vehicles of examples/parking held at a steering angle and a speed
// (check/circle.ent) stay on the circle the formula gives, within 0.01
// mm after 80 m, turn at full lock in their turning circle kerb to kerb,
// within 1 mm, and are where they are to the bit on one core and on all
// (parking-SPEC.md, check 1).
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/circle.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/circle.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: %python %S/../../examples/parking/check/circle.py %t.one %t.all | FileCheck %s

// CHECK: 20 vehicles: at most 0.00{{[0-9]+}} mm off their circles
// CHECK: ok
